{"hash":"d54cf3275b7067e7","voice":"en-IN-NeerjaExpressiveNeural","rate":"+4%","dur":66.905,"said":"Here, in the great hall, rests Nandi, the bull who carries Shiva. Look at where he looks. His eyes never leave the sanctum. In almost every Shiva temple Nandi waits like this, still and patient, facing his Lord: he is Shiva’s mount, and the guardian at the door of Kailash. The old teachers say his unbroken gaze is a lesson for you. The soul, like Nandi, is meant to keep its attention on the divine, however busy the hall around it becomes. Many devotees like to bend close and whisper a wish into Nandi’s ear, often the right one, trusting the faithful gatekeeper to carry it to his master. It is a loving custom, not a rule. If you wish, stand beside him and look where he looks, straight down the hall to the Jyotirlinga, and let your own gaze settle the same way. Then go on. You are only a few steps from the Lord now.\n\nDid you know? In many Shiva temples devotees whisper their prayers into Nandi’s ear, for him to carry to Shiva.","segments":[{"key":"text","start":0,"end":825},{"key":"didYouKnow","start":841,"end":938}],"words":[[0.098,0.421,0,4],[0.735,0.12,6,8],[0.867,0.084,9,12],[0.963,0.349,13,18],[1.324,0.409,19,23],[2.021,0.481,25,30],[2.514,0.505,31,36],[3.259,0.096,38,41],[3.367,0.288,42,46],[3.668,0.156,47,50],[3.836,0.421,51,58],[4.269,0.445,59,64],[5.637,0.252,66,70],[5.901,0.18,71,73],[6.094,0.204,74,79],[6.31,0.108,80,82],[6.43,0.445,83,88],[7.752,0.18,90,93],[7.945,0.252,94,98],[8.209,0.3,99,104],[8.522,0.228,105,110],[8.762,0.108,111,114],[8.882,0.649,115,122],[10.433,0.132,124,126],[10.577,0.505,127,133],[11.094,0.373,134,139],[11.478,0.361,140,145],[11.851,0.421,146,152],[12.284,0.373,153,158],[12.668,0.337,159,164],[13.017,0.216,165,169],[13.245,0.361,170,174],[13.81,0.276,176,181],[14.099,0.168,182,185],[14.279,0.565,186,193],[15.072,0.433,195,201],[15.517,0.192,202,205],[15.721,0.349,206,210],[16.322,0.12,212,214],[16.454,0.096,215,217],[16.562,0.541,